Remarks, 1. This theorem was previously known only for projective
algebraic manifolds [13]. The proof we have given, using general elliptic
operators, is the only one known at present for the general case.

2. For a complex manifold X, we know, by the Thom isomorphism in K-
theory, that K(TX) is a free K(X)-module generated by \,. In other words,
there is a single elliptic symbol which, ina sense, generates everything. It is
thus natural to replace the index homomorphism

